id onward movement of funds.\", \"reporting_entity_name\": \"Republic Trust Bank Ltd\", \"reporting_entity_type\": \"\", \"investigation_findings\": \"The analyst reviewed the merchant profile, recent transaction history, KYC records and system-generated alerts.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe merchant normally receives low-value retail payments below SGD 500. The reviewed transaction of SGD 9,850.00 was substantially above the normal range. No invoice, business contract or clear commercial reason was available to explain the payment.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe funds were subsequently transferred to an unrelated company shortly after receipt. The activity is inconsistent with the stated business profile and presents an elevated money laundering risk.\", \"recommendation_remarks\": \"File an STR because the transaction is unusually large, inconsistent with the merchant profile and lacks a clear economic purpose.\", \"reporting_officer_name\": \"Alice Tan\", \"subject_contact_number\": \"+65 9876 4321\", \"approved_by_designation\": \"STRO / Compliance Manager\", \"compliance_officer_name\": \"Daniel Lim\", \"compliance_contact_number\": \"+65 9123 4567\", \"other_supporting_evidence\": \"Transaction monitoring screenshots, merchant risk profile, alert history and internal review notes.\", \"approving_officer_signature\": \"MW\", \"reporting_officer_signature\": \"AT\", \"reporting_officer_designation\": \"Compliance Analyst\", \"date_of_birth_or_incorporation\": \"2022-08-15\"}'),(14,77,3,NULL,'STR-2026-77-1784722282709','Suspicious Transaction Report Draft\n\nREPORTING ENTITY\nReporting entity: Republic Trust Bank Ltd\nEntity type: Bank\nUEN: 202612345N\nBusiness address: 1 Marina Boulevard, #20-01, Singapore 018989\nCompliance officer: Daniel Lim\nCompliance email: daniel.lim@rtbank.com.sg\nCompliance contact: +65 9123 4567\n\nSUBJECT / MERCHANT\nSubject name: Chan Wei Ming\nMerchant name: Chan Chinatown Hawker Stall\nMerchant ID: MRC-BREADTALK-RAFFLES-CITY\nBusiness type: Food and Beverage Merchant\nIdentification number: 202245678K\nAccount number: RTB-8392014756\nNationality: Singapore\nSubject address: 335 Smith Street, #02-123, Chinatown Complex, Singapore 050335\nSubject contact: +65 9876 4321\n\nTRANSACTION\nTransaction ID: UWP-MRW1IUGR-16DVR\nAmount: 9850.00\nCurrency: SGD\nDate/time: 2026-07-21T10:34\nPayment method: Bank Transfer\nChannel: Mobile Application\nStatus: Completed\nOriginating country: Singapore\nDestination country: Singapore\nSource of funds: Multiple third-party transfers with no clear connection to the merchant\'s normal food and beverage sales.\nDestination of funds: Beneficiary account held by Apex Global Trading Pte Ltd, account 987-654-321.\n\nINVESTIGATION\nDetection method: Automated Transaction Monitoring System\nRisk level: High\nRisk score: 65\nRisk indicators: Unusually large transaction, Rapid movement of funds, Structuring or smurfing, High-risk merchant category, Transaction inconsistent with profile, Unclear economic purpose, Third-party fund transfer\nOther risk indicators: The transaction value was significantly higher than the merchant\'s normal daily sales and was followed by rapid onward movement of funds.\nInvestigation findings: The analyst reviewed the merchant profile, recent transaction history, KYC records and system-generated alerts.\r\n\r\nThe merchant normally receives low-value retail payments below SGD 500. The reviewed transaction of SGD 9,850.00 was substantially above the normal range. No invoice, business contract or clear commercial reason was available to explain the payment.\r\n\r\nThe funds were subsequently transferred to an unrelated company shortly after receipt. The activity is inconsistent with the stated business profile and presents an elevated money laundering risk.\nSupporting documents: Transaction history, Account statement, KYC records, Merchant profile, Internal investigation notes, System alert logs, Screenshots\nOther supporting evidence: Transaction monitoring screenshots, merchant risk profile, alert history and internal review notes.\nOther actions taken: The account was placed under enhanced monitoring and the case was escalated to the STRO for review.\n\nRECOMMENDATION\nRecommended action: File STR\nRecommendation remarks: File an STR because the transaction is unusually large, inconsistent with the merchant profile and lacks a clear economic purpose.\nEscalated to: Michael Wong, STRO\n\nSTR NARRATIVE\nDuring routine transaction monitoring, the system detected unusual activity involving Chan Chinatown Hawker Stall.\r\n\r\nA transaction of SGD 9,850.00 was received through a mobile banking transfer. The value was significantly higher than the merchant\'s normal transaction pattern and was inconsistent with the expected activity of a small food and beverage business.\r\n\r\nThe funds originated from multiple third parties with no clear relationship to the merchant. Shortly after receipt, the funds were transferred to another corporate beneficiary. The activity showed possible rapid movement of funds and an unclear economic purpose.\r\n\r\nThe monitoring system identified an unusually large transaction, activity inconsistent with the merchant profile, possible structuring, and an unexplained third-party transfer.\r\n\r\nBased on the available information, the transaction may involve money laundering, fraud, or another financial crime. The case is therefore recommended for escalation and filing of a Suspicious Transaction Report.','approved_by_stro','2026-07-22 12:11:22','2026-07-22 12:14:31','2026-07-22 12:14:31',NULL,NULL,1,'2026-07-22 12:14:31','{\"uen\": \"202612345N\", \"status\": \"pending_approval\", \"alert_id\": \"77\", \"currency\": \"SGD\", \"priority\": \"High\", \"risk_level\": \"High\", \"risk_score\": \"65\", \"merchant_id\": \"MRC-BREADTALK-RAFFLES-CITY\", \"nationality\": \"Singapore\", \"report_date\": \"2026-07-22\", \"review_date\": \"2026-07-22\", \"reviewed_by\": \"Alice Tan\", \"escalated_to\": \"Michael Wong, ST